<%#
  The board: an 8 by 8 CSS grid with Red at the bottom, every dark square a real button with
  an accessible label naming its number and its contents.

  Nothing here decides a rule. game.targets_by_square is the engine's answer for the whole
  board in one pass: it respects mandatory capture, it is empty once the match has finished,
  and while a jump sequence is pending it holds the locked square and nothing else, so a board
  rendered from it cannot offer an illegal selection. The selected square arrives as a plain
  URL parameter and is honoured only when the engine says that piece can move.

  With JavaScript off every square is a form: a destination posts one leg to the moves
  endpoint, one of your own movable pieces re-selects, and anything else clears the selection.
  With JavaScript on the board controller intercepts the click, keeps the selection in the
  page and posts the leg through the one hidden form below, so selecting costs no round trip.
  It also remembers whether the keyboard was on the board (the focusin and focusout actions
  below), because a Turbo Stream replaces this whole element and takes the focused square with
  it; without JavaScript there is no update to survive and nothing here applies.
%>
<%
  targets_by_square = game.targets_by_square
  # Playable means: this visitor holds the seat of the side to move, the match is running (not
  # waiting for an opponent and not over), and the engine still has moves. A waiting match, a
  # finished one and the opponent's turn in an online match all render the same board with
  # every square switched off, so no control on the page is dead and no click can be refused.
  # In hot-seat one browser holds both seats, so it is playable on both sides' turns.
  playable = match.playable_by?(seats) && !game.finished?
  selection =
    if !playable
      nil
    elsif game.pending?
      game.locked_square
    elsif targets_by_square.key?(selected)
      selected
    end
  targets = selection ? Array(targets_by_square[selection]) : []
  shown = game.display_position
  last_move = game.last_move
%>
<div id="<%= Match::BOARD_ID %>" class="board-zone" data-controller="board"
     data-action="click->board#click focusin->board#focusIn focusout->board#focusOut"
     data-board-selected-value="<%= selection %>"
     data-board-locked-value="<%= game.pending? %>">
  <div class="board" role="group" aria-label="Checkers board, Red at the bottom">
    <% board_cells.each do |number| %>
      <% if number.nil? %>
        <div class="board__cell board__cell--light" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <% else %>
        <%= render "matches/square", match: match, number: number, piece: shown.at(number),
              selection: selection, target: targets.include?(number),
              last_move_end: last_move_end(number, last_move&.origin, last_move&.destination),
              playable: playable, pending: game.pending?,
              own_targets: (targets_by_square[number] if playable) %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if playable %>
    <%= form_with url: match_moves_path(match), method: :post, class: "board__leg",
                  data: { board_target: "form" } do %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :from, nil, id: nil, data: { board_target: "from" } %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :to, nil, id: nil, data: { board_target: "to" } %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
